=== hive --help (ko)
Aigent Hive: AI 코딩 도구에 지침·지식·안전 장치를 더하는 로컬 도우미

사용법: hive <명령> [옵션]
명령별 옵션 표와 예시: hive <명령> --help
결과는 저장한 언어로 표시. 기계용 출력: --output json

시작하기
  install         사용자 환경에 Hive 설치·확인
  setup           처음 설정 또는 프로젝트 설정
  doctor          설치 상태 확인
  check-target    프로젝트 폴더 사용 가능 여부 확인

설정
  project         프로젝트 Hive 지침 갱신
  agent           사용자 정의 에이전트 관리
  role            역할 확인과 인계 기록
  roster          신 이름 목록과 역할 배정 보기
  summon          신 이름으로 기능 호출
  msg             역할 사이 메시지 보내기·받기
  stop            새 메시지 중지와 취소 요청
  <신 이름>       신 이름으로 Skill 기능 실행 (hive roster --help)

지식
  knowledge       지식 저장·검색·관리
  source-wiki     Hive 소스 위키 검사·검색
  index           지식 검색 색인 다시 만들기

갱신
  update          Hive 갱신 또는 새 버전 확인
  uninstall       사용자 환경에서 Hive 제거
  release         내려받은 릴리스 묶음 검증

진단
  usage           사용량 확인과 사용량 보호
  storage         Hive 저장 공간 측정
  prune           정리할 파일 미리 보기·삭제
  report          문제 보고 자료 만들기
  korean          한국어 출력 검사

고급
  session         자동 편집 세션 예약·확인
  run             작업 체크포인트·재개·종료 확인
  loop            반복 작업 그래프 관리
  orchestration   여러 작업 배정·조율
  judge           독립 검증 패키지·판정
  advanced        요청 경로 결정·프롬프트 검증 (에이전트용)
  hook            호스트 hook 처리 (호스트 전용)
  policy          정책 평가·hook 설정
  discord         Discord 알림 시험·수신

버전: hive --version

=== hive install --help (ko)
hive install: 사용자 환경에 Hive 설치·확인

사용자 폴더에 Hive를 설치하고 고른 AI 도구(호스트)에 연결.
먼저 --dry-run으로 바뀔 내용을 본 뒤 --apply로 적용.

필수 옵션
  --scope user                 설치 범위 (항상 user)
  --hosts <목록>               쉼표로 구분한 호스트 목록
                               codex, claude, antigravity 중 선택
                               또는 --host <호스트>를 여러 번
  --dry-run|--apply|--validate 미리 보기 | 적용 | 설치 확인

선택 옵션
  --recover                    중단된 설치 복구
  --user-root <폴더>           사용자 폴더 (기본: 홈 폴더)
  --output json                기계용 JSON 출력

예시
  hive install --scope user --hosts codex,claude --dry-run
  hive install --scope user --hosts codex,claude --apply

전체 형식
    hive install --scope user (--host codex|claude|antigravity)...|--hosts
        <comma-separated-hosts> (--dry-run|--apply|--validate) [--user-root
        <dir>] [--output json]

=== hive setup --help (ko)
hive setup: 처음 설정 또는 프로젝트 설정

옵션 없이 실행하면 사용자 전역 설정을 질문으로 진행.
--target을 주면 그 프로젝트 폴더를 설정.

필수 옵션
  --target <폴더>              설정할 프로젝트 폴더 (프로젝트 설정)

선택 옵션
  --user-root <폴더>           사용자 폴더 (기본: 홈 폴더)
  --interactive                터미널에서 질문으로 진행
  --non-interactive            질문 없이 진행
  --resume                     중단한 설정 이어서 진행
  --show [--summary]           현재 설정 보기 (짧은 요약)
  --describe --section <id>    설정 항목 설명 보기
  --answers <yml>              답변 파일로 설정 (모드 필요)
  --dry-run|--apply|--validate 미리 보기 | 적용 | 확인
  --capabilities <json>        호스트 기능 정보 파일
  --output json                기계용 JSON 출력

예시
  hive setup
  hive setup --target .
  hive setup --target . --show

전체 형식
    hive setup --target <dir> [--user-root <dir>]
        [--interactive|--non-interactive] [--resume|--dry-run]
    hive setup --target <dir> [--user-root <dir>] (--show|--describe --section
        <id>) [--output json]
    hive setup --target <dir> --user-root <dir> --show --summary [--output json]
    hive setup --target <dir> --user-root <dir> --describe --question
        <question-id> [--output json]
    hive setup --target <dir> --answers <yml> [--capabilities <json>]
        --user-root <dir> (--dry-run|--apply|--validate) [--reconfigure-role
        <role-id>]... [--input-channel answers-file|agent] [--output json]

전역 설정의 전체 형식: hive setup --scope user --help

MODES:
    --summary    Compact status/completion output; not an approval preview
    --dry-run    Render and validate in staging without changing the target
    --apply      Render, validate, and apply only manifest-owned changes
    --validate   Validate the installed harness without changing the target

--capabilities is optional for --dry-run, --apply and --validate. Without it,
file setup uses the same saved or detected host capability data as terminal
setup; no command generates a capability file. Detection never verifies
execution support or grants hooks.

=== hive update --help (ko)
hive update: Hive 갱신 또는 새 버전 확인

설치한 Hive와 사용자 환경 연결을 새 버전으로 갱신.
기본 채널은 stable. 시험판은 --channel test를 직접 지정.

필수 옵션
  없음

선택 옵션
  --channel stable|test        갱신 채널 (기본 stable)
  --confirm                    소프트웨어 갱신만 승인
                               설정 질문에는 답하지 않음
  --interactive                터미널에서 질문 (JSON과 함께 불가)
  --non-interactive            입력을 기다리지 않음
  --check                      설치 없이 새 버전만 확인
  --user-root <폴더>           사용자 폴더 (--check에는 필수)
  --output json                기계용 JSON 출력

예시
  hive update
  hive update --channel test --confirm
  hive update --check --user-root <user-root>

전체 형식
    hive update [--channel stable|test] [--user-root <absolute-dir>] [--confirm]
        [--interactive|--non-interactive] [--output json]
    hive update --check --user-root <absolute-dir> [--output json]
    hive update --target <dir> --bundle <release-dir> (--dry-run|--apply)
        [--output json]
    hive update --target <dir> --recover [--output json]
    hive update --target <dir> --bundle <release-dir> --apply
        --exact-major-target <X.Y.Z> --major-confirmation <confirmation.json>
        [--output json]

=== hive knowledge --help (ko)
hive knowledge: 지식 저장·검색·관리

프로젝트와 사용자 지식을 Markdown 원본으로 저장하고 검색.
하위 명령 하나의 형식: hive knowledge <하위 명령> --help
주요 하위 명령: remember, retrieve, query, list, read, lint,
export, import, transfer, scan, graph, vector

필수 옵션
  --target <폴더>              대상 프로젝트 폴더 (대부분)
  --user-root <폴더>           사용자 폴더 (remember, retrieve 등)

선택 옵션
  --text <검색어>              검색어 (query)
  --query <검색어>             검색어 (retrieve)
  --limit <1..100>             결과 수 제한
  --output json                기계용 JSON 출력

예시
  hive knowledge lint --target .
  hive knowledge query --target . --text build
  hive knowledge retrieve --user-root <user-root> --target . --query build

전체 형식
    hive knowledge ingest --target <dir> --source <file> --wiki <draft.md>
        [--user-root <dir>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge add --target <dir> --source <file> --wiki <draft.md>
        [--quick] [--user-root <dir>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge query --target <dir> (--text <query>|--tag <tag>|--category
        <category>) [--limit <1..100>] [--user-root <dir>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge list --target <dir> [--tag <tag>] [--category <category>]
        [--limit <1..100>] [--user-root <dir>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge read --target <dir> --page-id <id> [--user-root <dir>]
        [--output json]
    hive knowledge promote --target <project> --user-root <dir> --page-id <id>
        --category fact|preference|workflow (--dry-run|--apply) [--output json]
    hive knowledge promote --user-root <dir> --collection <id-or-alias>
        [--review-id <id>] --dry-run [--output json]
    hive knowledge promote --user-root <dir> --collection <id-or-alias>
        --review-id <id> --expected-source-digest <sha256:...>
        --confirm-global-promotion --apply [--output json]
    hive knowledge lint --target <dir> [--user-root <dir>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge delete --target <dir> --page-id <id> --reason <text>
        [--replacement <locator>] --timestamp <RFC3339> [--user-root <dir>]
        [--output json]
    hive knowledge suppress --target <dir> --fingerprint <sha256:...>
        --source-locator <locator> --reason <text> [--replacement <locator>]
        --timestamp <RFC3339> [--user-root <dir>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge remember --user-root <dir> (--request
        <request.json>|--user-statement <normalized-fact> --claim-key
        <stable-key> [--kind
        project-profile|decision|convention|preference|workflow] [--subject
        <area/topic>]|--batch <facts.json>) [--output json]
    hive knowledge retrieve --user-root <dir> --target <current-dir> (--request
        <request.json>|--query <text> [--scope <scope>] [--top-k <1..100>]
        [--byte-budget <bytes>] [--expansions "<term,term>"]) [--mode
        fts|semantic] [--authorization-id <id> --authorization-token <token>
        --capabilities <json> --usage <json>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge subjects list --user-root <dir> [--collection user-root]
        [--output json]
    hive knowledge subjects preview --user-root <dir> [--collection user-root]
        [--limit <0..1000>] [--offset <n>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge subjects apply --user-root <dir> --review <review.json>
        --confirm-subject-assignment yes [--output json]
    hive knowledge subjects restore --user-root <dir> --operation <id>
        --confirm-subject-restore yes [--output json]
    hive knowledge authorize-confidential --user-root <dir> --target
        <current-dir> --collection <id-or-alias> --query <text> --capabilities
        <json> --usage <json> --expires-at <unix-seconds> --nonce <nonce>
        --confirm-current-action [--output json]
    hive knowledge authorize-collection --user-root <dir> --operation
        attach|map|detach --collection <id-or-alias> [--target <dir>]
        --expires-at <unix-seconds> --nonce <nonce> --confirm-current-action
        [--output json]
    hive knowledge collection attach|map --user-root <dir> --collection
        <id-or-alias> --target <dir> --authorization-id <id>
        --authorization-token <token> [--output json]
    hive knowledge collection detach --user-root <dir> --collection
        <id-or-alias> --authorization-id <id> --authorization-token <token>
        [--output json]
    hive knowledge scan --target <dir> (--inventory|--candidates
        <review.json>|--apply <review.json>) [--include-untracked]
        [--prior-inventory <json>] [--user-root <dir>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge export --user-root <dir> --scope
        global|shared|project:<id>|collection:<id>|all-portable --bundle
        <path>.hivekb [--replace-backup <file-name>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge import --user-root <dir> --bundle <path>.hivekb
        (--dry-run|--apply) [--output json]
    hive knowledge transfer export --preview|--apply --user-root <dir> --scope
        global|shared|project:<id>|collection:<id>|all-portable --bundle
        <path>.hivekb [--replace-backup <file-name>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge transfer import --preview|--apply [--exclude-conflicts]
        [--preview-digest <sha256:...> --expected-sha256 <sha256:...>]
        --user-root <dir> --bundle <path>.hivekb [--output json]
    hive knowledge transfer merge preview --bundle <path>.hivekb --bundle
        <path>.hivekb [--user-root <dir>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge transfer merge review|apply --bundle <path>.hivekb --bundle
        <path>.hivekb --preview-digest <sha256:...> --review <review.json>
        [--review-digest <sha256:...>] [--user-root <dir>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge transfer status --id <transfer-id> [--user-root <dir>]
        [--output json]
    hive knowledge transfer vector --id <transfer-id> --receipt-digest
        <sha256:...> --answer yes|no|cancel [--user-root <dir>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge refresh (--target <legacy-project>|--user-root <dir>)
        [--output json]
    hive knowledge graph preview|enable|status|rebuild|disable|query|export
        --target <dir> [--scope project] [--engine
        native-markdown|graphify-code] [--consent-digest <sha256:...>] [--input
        <graph.json> --receipt <receipt.json>] [--node-id <id>] [--text <query>]
        [--user-root <dir>] [--format json|html] [--output json]
    hive knowledge graph preview|enable|disable|status|prepare|apply|query
        --engine host-semantic --target <dir> --user-root <dir> --collection
        <id> --visibility shared|project-private|confidential --host
        codex|antigravity [--consent-digest <digest>] [--request-digest <digest>
        --input <result.json> --receipt <receipt.json>] [--node-id <id>]
        [--output json]

=== hive knowledge retrieve --help (ko)
hive knowledge retrieve

형식
    hive knowledge retrieve --user-root <dir> --target <current-dir> (--request
        <request.json>|--query <text> [--scope <scope>] [--top-k <1..100>]
        [--byte-budget <bytes>] [--expansions "<term,term>"]) [--mode
        fts|semantic] [--authorization-id <id> --authorization-token <token>
        --capabilities <json> --usage <json>] [--output json]

예시
  hive knowledge retrieve --user-root <user-root> --target . --query build

전체 지식 명령: hive knowledge --help

=== hive usage --help (ko)
hive usage: 사용량 확인과 사용량 보호

AI 도구 사용량을 확인하고, 남은 양이 기준보다 적으면 작업을 멈춤.
하위 명령: show, status, threshold, session, monitor, enforce,
check, probe-native, capture, summarize-tokens, fallback-install

필수 옵션
  --user-root <폴더>           사용자 폴더 (show, threshold, monitor)
  --target <폴더>              프로젝트 폴더 (status, enforce, session)
  --session-id <id>            현재 세션 id (status, enforce, session)
  --process-id <번호>          현재 프로세스 번호 (위와 같음)

선택 옵션
  --host <호스트>              codex, claude, antigravity 중 하나
  --remaining-percent <0..99>  모든 보호 한도의 남은 양 기준 % (threshold)
  --output json                기계용 JSON 출력

예시
  hive usage threshold --user-root <user-root> --remaining-percent 20
  hive usage monitor status --user-root <user-root>

전체 형식
    hive usage check --account-digest <sha256:...> [--threshold <0..99>]
        [--output json]
    hive usage probe-native --host codex|claude|antigravity [--output json]
    hive usage monitor preview|enable|disable|status --user-root <dir> [--output
        json]
    hive usage enforce --target <dir> --session-id <id> --process-id
        <positive-u32> [--host codex|claude|antigravity] [--account-digest
        <sha256:...>] [--user-root <dir>] [--output json]
    hive usage status --target <dir> --session-id <id> --process-id
        <positive-u32> [--host codex|claude|antigravity] [--user-root <dir>]
        [--output json]
    hive usage threshold (--target <configured-project>|--user-root <user-root>)
        --remaining-percent <0..99> [--output json]
    hive usage session --target <dir> --session-id <id> --process-id
        <positive-u32> [--host codex|claude|antigravity] [--user-root <dir>]
        --action enable|disable|toggle [--confirm-session-disable] [--output
        json]
    hive usage capture --host claude|antigravity (--target
        <dir>|--target-from-stdin) --stdin-json [--output json]
    hive usage summarize-tokens --request <normalized-events.json> [--output
        json]
    hive usage fallback-install --host codex|claude|antigravity
        (--dry-run|--apply) [--confirm-install] [--output json]

=== hive project upgrade --help (ko)
hive project upgrade: 프로젝트 Hive 지침 갱신

설치한 프로젝트 하네스를 현재 Hive 버전에 맞게 갱신.
사용자가 고친 내용은 보존. 먼저 --scan 또는 --dry-run으로 확인.

필수 옵션
  --target <폴더>              갱신할 프로젝트 폴더
  --scan|--dry-run|--apply     검사 | 미리 보기 | 적용
  --validate|--recover         또는 확인 | 복구 중 하나

선택 옵션
  --user-root <폴더>           사용자 폴더 (기본: 홈 폴더)
  --skill-merge-inputs <skill> Skill 병합 입력 보기
  --skill-merges <json>        Skill 병합 결과 파일
  --approve-skill-merge <digest>
                               확인한 병합 승인
  --output json                기계용 JSON 출력

예시
  hive project upgrade --target . --scan
  hive project upgrade --target . --dry-run
  hive project upgrade --target . --apply

전체 형식
    hive project upgrade --target <dir>
        (--scan|--dry-run|--apply|--validate|--recover) [--skill-merge-inputs
        <skill>|--skill-merges <json> --approve-skill-merge <digest>] [--output
        json]

=== hive --help (en)
Aigent Hive: a local helper that adds rules, knowledge and safety to AI tools

Usage: hive <command> [options]
Options and examples for one command: hive <command> --help
Results use your saved language. Machine output: --output json

Getting started
  install         Install or check Hive for your user
  setup           First-time or project setup
  doctor          Inspect the installation
  check-target    Check a project folder

Configuration
  project         Upgrade a project's Hive harness
  agent           Manage custom agents
  role            Validate roles and record handoffs
  roster          Show named roles and assignments
  summon          Call a function by its named role
  msg             Send and read role messages
  stop            Stop new messages and request cancel
  <god>           Run a Skill by its named role (hive roster --help)

Knowledge
  knowledge       Save, find and manage knowledge
  source-wiki     Check or search the Hive source Wiki
  index           Rebuild the knowledge index

Updates
  update          Update Hive or check for a new version
  uninstall       Remove Hive from your user
  release         Verify a downloaded release bundle

Diagnostics
  usage           Check usage and the usage guard
  storage         Measure Hive storage
  prune           Preview or remove old files
  report          Prepare a problem report
  korean          Check Korean output

Advanced
  session         Reserve or check edit sessions
  run             Checkpoint, resume or close work
  loop            Manage loop work graphs
  orchestration   Assign and coordinate work
  judge           Package and judge independent checks
  advanced        Route requests or check prompts (for agents)
  hook            Handle host hooks (hosts only)
  policy          Evaluate policy or configure hooks
  discord         Test or receive Discord notices

Version: hive --version

=== hive install --help (en)
hive install: install or check Hive for your user

Installs Hive in your user folder and connects the chosen AI tools (hosts).
Preview with --dry-run first, then apply with --apply.

Required options
  --scope user                 Install scope (always user)
  --hosts <목록>               Comma-separated hosts
                               Choose from codex, claude, antigravity
                               Or repeat --host <host>
  --dry-run|--apply|--validate Preview | apply | check the install

Optional
  --recover                    Recover an interrupted install
  --user-root <폴더>           User folder (default: home)
  --output json                Machine-readable JSON output

Examples
  hive install --scope user --hosts codex,claude --dry-run
  hive install --scope user --hosts codex,claude --apply

Full syntax
    hive install --scope user (--host codex|claude|antigravity)...|--hosts
        <comma-separated-hosts> (--dry-run|--apply|--validate) [--user-root
        <dir>] [--output json]

=== hive setup --help (en)
hive setup: first-time or project setup

Without options, asks the questions for your global user setup.
With --target, sets up that project folder.

Required options
  --target <폴더>              Project folder (project setup)

Optional
  --user-root <폴더>           User folder (default: home)
  --interactive                Ask questions in the terminal
  --non-interactive            Never wait for input
  --resume                     Continue an interrupted setup
  --show [--summary]           Show the setup (short summary)
  --describe --section <id>    Describe one setup section
  --answers <yml>              Use an answers file (needs a mode)
  --dry-run|--apply|--validate Preview | apply | validate
  --capabilities <json>        Host capability file
  --output json                Machine-readable JSON output

Examples
  hive setup
  hive setup --target .
  hive setup --target . --show

Full syntax
    hive setup --target <dir> [--user-root <dir>]
        [--interactive|--non-interactive] [--resume|--dry-run]
    hive setup --target <dir> [--user-root <dir>] (--show|--describe --section
        <id>) [--output json]
    hive setup --target <dir> --user-root <dir> --show --summary [--output json]
    hive setup --target <dir> --user-root <dir> --describe --question
        <question-id> [--output json]
    hive setup --target <dir> --answers <yml> [--capabilities <json>]
        --user-root <dir> (--dry-run|--apply|--validate) [--reconfigure-role
        <role-id>]... [--input-channel answers-file|agent] [--output json]

Global user setup syntax: hive setup --scope user --help

MODES:
    --summary    Compact status/completion output; not an approval preview
    --dry-run    Render and validate in staging without changing the target
    --apply      Render, validate, and apply only manifest-owned changes
    --validate   Validate the installed harness without changing the target

--capabilities is optional for --dry-run, --apply and --validate. Without it,
file setup uses the same saved or detected host capability data as terminal
setup; no command generates a capability file. Detection never verifies
execution support or grants hooks.

=== hive update --help (en)
hive update: update Hive or check for a new version

Updates the installed Hive package and its user connections.
The default channel is stable. The test channel needs --channel test.

Required options
  None

Optional
  --channel stable|test        Update channel (default stable)
  --confirm                    Accept only the software update
                               Does not answer setup questions
  --interactive                Ask in the terminal (not with JSON)
  --non-interactive            Never wait for input
  --check                      Only check for a newer version
  --user-root <폴더>           User folder (required with --check)
  --output json                Machine-readable JSON output

Examples
  hive update
  hive update --channel test --confirm
  hive update --check --user-root <user-root>

Full syntax
    hive update [--channel stable|test] [--user-root <absolute-dir>] [--confirm]
        [--interactive|--non-interactive] [--output json]
    hive update --check --user-root <absolute-dir> [--output json]
    hive update --target <dir> --bundle <release-dir> (--dry-run|--apply)
        [--output json]
    hive update --target <dir> --recover [--output json]
    hive update --target <dir> --bundle <release-dir> --apply
        --exact-major-target <X.Y.Z> --major-confirmation <confirmation.json>
        [--output json]

=== hive knowledge --help (en)
hive knowledge: save, find and manage knowledge

Saves and finds project and user knowledge as canonical Markdown.
One subcommand's syntax: hive knowledge <subcommand> --help
Main subcommands: remember, retrieve, query, list, read, lint,
export, import, transfer, scan, graph, vector

Required options
  --target <폴더>              Project folder (most subcommands)
  --user-root <폴더>           User folder (remember, retrieve, ...)

Optional
  --text <검색어>              Search text (query)
  --query <검색어>             Search text (retrieve)
  --limit <1..100>             Result limit
  --output json                Machine-readable JSON output

Examples
  hive knowledge lint --target .
  hive knowledge query --target . --text build
  hive knowledge retrieve --user-root <user-root> --target . --query build

Full syntax
    hive knowledge ingest --target <dir> --source <file> --wiki <draft.md>
        [--user-root <dir>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge add --target <dir> --source <file> --wiki <draft.md>
        [--quick] [--user-root <dir>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge query --target <dir> (--text <query>|--tag <tag>|--category
        <category>) [--limit <1..100>] [--user-root <dir>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge list --target <dir> [--tag <tag>] [--category <category>]
        [--limit <1..100>] [--user-root <dir>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge read --target <dir> --page-id <id> [--user-root <dir>]
        [--output json]
    hive knowledge promote --target <project> --user-root <dir> --page-id <id>
        --category fact|preference|workflow (--dry-run|--apply) [--output json]
    hive knowledge promote --user-root <dir> --collection <id-or-alias>
        [--review-id <id>] --dry-run [--output json]
    hive knowledge promote --user-root <dir> --collection <id-or-alias>
        --review-id <id> --expected-source-digest <sha256:...>
        --confirm-global-promotion --apply [--output json]
    hive knowledge lint --target <dir> [--user-root <dir>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge delete --target <dir> --page-id <id> --reason <text>
        [--replacement <locator>] --timestamp <RFC3339> [--user-root <dir>]
        [--output json]
    hive knowledge suppress --target <dir> --fingerprint <sha256:...>
        --source-locator <locator> --reason <text> [--replacement <locator>]
        --timestamp <RFC3339> [--user-root <dir>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge remember --user-root <dir> (--request
        <request.json>|--user-statement <normalized-fact> --claim-key
        <stable-key> [--kind
        project-profile|decision|convention|preference|workflow] [--subject
        <area/topic>]|--batch <facts.json>) [--output json]
    hive knowledge retrieve --user-root <dir> --target <current-dir> (--request
        <request.json>|--query <text> [--scope <scope>] [--top-k <1..100>]
        [--byte-budget <bytes>] [--expansions "<term,term>"]) [--mode
        fts|semantic] [--authorization-id <id> --authorization-token <token>
        --capabilities <json> --usage <json>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge subjects list --user-root <dir> [--collection user-root]
        [--output json]
    hive knowledge subjects preview --user-root <dir> [--collection user-root]
        [--limit <0..1000>] [--offset <n>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge subjects apply --user-root <dir> --review <review.json>
        --confirm-subject-assignment yes [--output json]
    hive knowledge subjects restore --user-root <dir> --operation <id>
        --confirm-subject-restore yes [--output json]
    hive knowledge authorize-confidential --user-root <dir> --target
        <current-dir> --collection <id-or-alias> --query <text> --capabilities
        <json> --usage <json> --expires-at <unix-seconds> --nonce <nonce>
        --confirm-current-action [--output json]
    hive knowledge authorize-collection --user-root <dir> --operation
        attach|map|detach --collection <id-or-alias> [--target <dir>]
        --expires-at <unix-seconds> --nonce <nonce> --confirm-current-action
        [--output json]
    hive knowledge collection attach|map --user-root <dir> --collection
        <id-or-alias> --target <dir> --authorization-id <id>
        --authorization-token <token> [--output json]
    hive knowledge collection detach --user-root <dir> --collection
        <id-or-alias> --authorization-id <id> --authorization-token <token>
        [--output json]
    hive knowledge scan --target <dir> (--inventory|--candidates
        <review.json>|--apply <review.json>) [--include-untracked]
        [--prior-inventory <json>] [--user-root <dir>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge export --user-root <dir> --scope
        global|shared|project:<id>|collection:<id>|all-portable --bundle
        <path>.hivekb [--replace-backup <file-name>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge import --user-root <dir> --bundle <path>.hivekb
        (--dry-run|--apply) [--output json]
    hive knowledge transfer export --preview|--apply --user-root <dir> --scope
        global|shared|project:<id>|collection:<id>|all-portable --bundle
        <path>.hivekb [--replace-backup <file-name>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge transfer import --preview|--apply [--exclude-conflicts]
        [--preview-digest <sha256:...> --expected-sha256 <sha256:...>]
        --user-root <dir> --bundle <path>.hivekb [--output json]
    hive knowledge transfer merge preview --bundle <path>.hivekb --bundle
        <path>.hivekb [--user-root <dir>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge transfer merge review|apply --bundle <path>.hivekb --bundle
        <path>.hivekb --preview-digest <sha256:...> --review <review.json>
        [--review-digest <sha256:...>] [--user-root <dir>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge transfer status --id <transfer-id> [--user-root <dir>]
        [--output json]
    hive knowledge transfer vector --id <transfer-id> --receipt-digest
        <sha256:...> --answer yes|no|cancel [--user-root <dir>] [--output json]
    hive knowledge refresh (--target <legacy-project>|--user-root <dir>)
        [--output json]
    hive knowledge graph preview|enable|status|rebuild|disable|query|export
        --target <dir> [--scope project] [--engine
        native-markdown|graphify-code] [--consent-digest <sha256:...>] [--input
        <graph.json> --receipt <receipt.json>] [--node-id <id>] [--text <query>]
        [--user-root <dir>] [--format json|html] [--output json]
    hive knowledge graph preview|enable|disable|status|prepare|apply|query
        --engine host-semantic --target <dir> --user-root <dir> --collection
        <id> --visibility shared|project-private|confidential --host
        codex|antigravity [--consent-digest <digest>] [--request-digest <digest>
        --input <result.json> --receipt <receipt.json>] [--node-id <id>]
        [--output json]

=== hive knowledge retrieve --help (en)
hive knowledge retrieve

Syntax
    hive knowledge retrieve --user-root <dir> --target <current-dir> (--request
        <request.json>|--query <text> [--scope <scope>] [--top-k <1..100>]
        [--byte-budget <bytes>] [--expansions "<term,term>"]) [--mode
        fts|semantic] [--authorization-id <id> --authorization-token <token>
        --capabilities <json> --usage <json>] [--output json]

Example
  hive knowledge retrieve --user-root <user-root> --target . --query build

All knowledge commands: hive knowledge --help

=== hive usage --help (en)
hive usage: check usage and the usage guard

Checks AI tool usage and stops work when too little remains.
Subcommands: show, status, threshold, session, monitor, enforce,
check, probe-native, capture, summarize-tokens, fallback-install

Required options
  --user-root <폴더>           User folder (show, threshold, monitor)
  --target <폴더>              Project folder (status, enforce, session)
  --session-id <id>            Current session id (same)
  --process-id <번호>          Current process id (same)

Optional
  --host <호스트>              One of codex, claude, antigravity
  --remaining-percent <0..99>  Threshold %, all guarded limits (threshold)
  --output json                Machine-readable JSON output

Examples
  hive usage threshold --user-root <user-root> --remaining-percent 20
  hive usage monitor status --user-root <user-root>

Full syntax
    hive usage check --account-digest <sha256:...> [--threshold <0..99>]
        [--output json]
    hive usage probe-native --host codex|claude|antigravity [--output json]
    hive usage monitor preview|enable|disable|status --user-root <dir> [--output
        json]
    hive usage enforce --target <dir> --session-id <id> --process-id
        <positive-u32> [--host codex|claude|antigravity] [--account-digest
        <sha256:...>] [--user-root <dir>] [--output json]
    hive usage status --target <dir> --session-id <id> --process-id
        <positive-u32> [--host codex|claude|antigravity] [--user-root <dir>]
        [--output json]
    hive usage threshold (--target <configured-project>|--user-root <user-root>)
        --remaining-percent <0..99> [--output json]
    hive usage session --target <dir> --session-id <id> --process-id
        <positive-u32> [--host codex|claude|antigravity] [--user-root <dir>]
        --action enable|disable|toggle [--confirm-session-disable] [--output
        json]
    hive usage capture --host claude|antigravity (--target
        <dir>|--target-from-stdin) --stdin-json [--output json]
    hive usage summarize-tokens --request <normalized-events.json> [--output
        json]
    hive usage fallback-install --host codex|claude|antigravity
        (--dry-run|--apply) [--confirm-install] [--output json]

=== hive project upgrade --help (en)
hive project upgrade: upgrade a project's Hive harness

Upgrades an installed project harness to this Hive version.
Your edits are kept. Check with --scan or --dry-run first.

Required options
  --target <폴더>              Project folder to upgrade
  --scan|--dry-run|--apply     Scan | preview | apply
  --validate|--recover         Or validate | recover

Optional
  --user-root <폴더>           User folder (default: home)
  --skill-merge-inputs <skill> Show Skill merge inputs
  --skill-merges <json>        Skill merge result file
  --approve-skill-merge <digest>
                               Approve the reviewed merge
  --output json                Machine-readable JSON output

Examples
  hive project upgrade --target . --scan
  hive project upgrade --target . --dry-run
  hive project upgrade --target . --apply

Full syntax
    hive project upgrade --target <dir>
        (--scan|--dry-run|--apply|--validate|--recover) [--skill-merge-inputs
        <skill>|--skill-merges <json> --approve-skill-merge <digest>] [--output
        json]
